588 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Splitting the dataset into training and testing subsets is less common in association rule mining than it is in methods like supervised learning. Generally, association rule mining entails examining the complete dataset to identify recurring item groups and produce significant rules. Rather than making predictions or modeling data that hasn't been seen yet, the emphasis is on finding patterns and relationships within the entire data set. But in some situations, researchers might use hold-out samples or cross-validation to assess how robustly found rules hold up.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
