/E (We started the data cleaning process by systematically removing all extraneous whitespace to ensure the integrity and uniformity of the dataset. This meticulous cleaning was vital as even minor inconsistencies can lead to misleading results in later analyses. After this, I converted all categorical columns into factors, which is an essential step in R for handling categorical data effectively and facilitating proper statistical analysis.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
613 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Once the data was formatted correctly, I transformed the cleaned dataset into a 'transactions' object in R. This transformation is crucial for applying the Apriori rule mining algorithm, as it organises the data into a structure suitable for identifying frequent item sets and association rules. During the pre-processing phase, I paid careful attention to the conversion of each categorical column into factors, ensuring that all levels were accurately represented, and any potential discrepancies were addressed. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
