641 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The Apriori algorithm was executed with specific parameters to analyse the dataset effectively. The minimum support threshold was set at 0.1%, ensuring that only item sets appearing in at least 0.1% of all transactions were considered significant. Additionally, a minimum confidence level of 95% was established, indicating that the generated rules should be highly reliable. The analysis focused on rule lengths between 2 and 5 items, allowing for a diverse range of associations to be explored.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
642 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
643 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (As a result of these parameters, a total of 2,624 association rules were generated. These rules exhibited notably high lift values, suggesting strong positive correlations among various attributes in the dataset. For instance, the association rules relating to the Region and Sales Channel frequently emerged with high confidence levels. This consistent correlation implies that certain sales channels are strongly preferred in specific regions, providing valuable insights for strategic decision-making in marketing and distribution. Apriori algorithm was executed with the following parameters: minimum support 0.1%, minimum confidence 95%, and rule length between 2 and 5 items. 2,624 rules were generated.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
