747 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This study effectively demonstrates the capabilities of association rule mining in revealing valuable insights from sales transactional data. Among the key findings, the prevalence of cosmetics in online purchases within Sub-Saharan Africa emerged as a noteworthy trend, while the high demand for fruits in the Middle Eastern market was also highlighted.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
748 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E ( )
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
749 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (These insights are instrumental not only for optimising regional inventory management and enhancing demand forecasting but also for informing the development of targeted marketing campaigns. For example, the understanding that cosmetics enjoy significant online sales in Sub-Saharan Africa provides critical intelligence for crafting specialised digital marketing strategies and promotional activities tailored to this demographic.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
750 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Furthermore, the process of rule pruning contributed to a more refined analysis by minimising redundancy, thus improving both the interpretability and clarity of the results. This methodological approach allows decision-makers to prioritise and focus on the most impactful rules, enhancing their strategic planning capabilities. Future investigations could delve into various aspects, such as temporal trends, seasonal fluctuations, or the interplay between pricing strategies and profit margins, thereby generating even more comprehensive insights.)
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
