795 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The 10000 Sales Records dataset was utilized for a classification task to predict international sales transaction profitability. The dataset consists of 10,000 rows and 14 columns, each representing some specific operational or financial attribute of individual sales records. The dataset simulates transactions in different countries, product categories, sales channels, and order priorities. All the values in the data set are whole and do not contain any missing values, making sure that the integrity and consistency required for valid data analysis is provided.)
/Pg 44 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
796 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (The 14 variables of the data set are listed below:)
/E (The 14 variables of the data set are listed below:)
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
797 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (1. Region: Geographical area where the sale was executed 2. Country: Individual country where the transaction was conducted 3. Item Type: Category of item sold \(e.g., Fruits, Clothing, Electronics\) 4. Sales Channel: Channel of distribution used  \(Online = 1, Offline = 0 5. Order Priority: Urgency level of the order \(High, Medium, Low\) 6. Order Date: Order placement date 7. Order ID: Order's individual number 8. Units Sold: Total number of units sold in the transaction 9. Unit Price: Sale price per unit 10. Unit Cost: Unit price per unit 11. Total Revenue: Overall revenue derived from the transaction 12. Total Cost: Overall cost spent on the transaction 13. Total Profit: Derived net profit \(Total Revenue - Total Cost\) 14. Profitability Label: Binary profitability label        \(Profitable = 1, Not Profitable = 0\) This is the dependent variable  )
/E (1. Region: Geographical area where the sale was executed 2. Country: Individual country where the transaction was conducted 3. Item Type: Category of item sold \(e.g., Fruits, Clothing, Electronics\) 4. Sales Channel: Channel of distribution used  \(Online = 1, Offline = 0 5. Order Priority: Urgency level of the order \(High, Medium, Low\) 6. Order Date: Order placement date 7. Order ID: Order's individual number 8. Units Sold: Total number of units sold in the transaction 9. Unit Price: Sale price per unit 10. Unit Cost: Unit price per unit 11. Total Revenue: Overall revenue derived from the transaction 12. Total Cost: Overall cost spent on the transaction 13. Total Profit: Derived net profit \(Total Revenue - Total Cost\) 14. Profitability Label: Binary profitability label        \(Profitable = 1, Not Profitable = 0\) This is the dependent variable  )
/Pg 45 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
