/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Logistic regression is among the most widely used binary classification algorithms applied in data mining. Logistic regression gives a probabilistic way of modelling interaction between input variables and categorical output, and as such, it is extremely applicable in business purposes such as profitability prediction and forecasting sales. Logistic regression here is applied to construct a binary classification model for predicting the probability that a transaction is profitable based on operational and financial variables.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
805 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The goal of employing logistic regression with this data is to develop a predictive model to assist businesses with identifying significant patterns pertaining to successful and unsuccessful profits. By looking at variables such as region, item type, sales channel, order priority, units sold, unit cost, and unit price, the model can identify hidden patterns that are responsible for determining profit results. This insight can then be utilized to drive data-based decision-making in business fields such as price strategy, geographic targeting, inventory planning, and resource allocation resulting in business performance and profitability enhancement.)
/Pg 47 0 R
/K [0]
>>
