923 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/T (2.10.  CONCLUSION The 10,000 Sales Records data allowed the creation of a logistic regression model that exposed crucial drivers of profitability. Total Profit variations strongly related to Unit Price along with Units Sold and Unit Cost thus assisting in detecting profitable and non-profitable business deals. Performance checks through accuracy metrics and other measurements enabled the model validation through training testing ratio splits of 70% to 30%. The evaluation confirmed strong prediction capabilities and cross-applicability of the model. This analysis establishes that data-driven models in combination with visual tools enhance pricing alongside sales and cost decision-making across business operations.  )
/E (2.10.  CONCLUSION The 10,000 Sales Records data allowed the creation of a logistic regression model that exposed crucial drivers of profitability. Total Profit variations strongly related to Unit Price along with Units Sold and Unit Cost thus assisting in detecting profitable and non-profitable business deals. Performance checks through accuracy metrics and other measurements enabled the model validation through training testing ratio splits of 70% to 30%. The evaluation confirmed strong prediction capabilities and cross-applicability of the model. This analysis establishes that data-driven models in combination with visual tools enhance pricing alongside sales and cost decision-making across business operations.  )
/Pg 67 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
